  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">District Cooling in San Jos&#xE9;, Costa Rica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project delivers demand-led technical assistance to the Costa Rican Electricity Institute (ICE) to design and finance district cooling solutions for San Jose&amp;rsquo;s buildings.The distric cooling solutions will replace the individual cooling systems using CFC and HFC with centralized system which will be more efficient and willl use natural refrigerants.The project will work in the following workstreams:1.Development of policy recommendations to promote district cooling to be included in Costa Rica National District Cooling Strategy2.Identification of advanced refrigeration and/or cooling technologies and applications3.Development of bankable business models for district cooling solutions4.Design of a climate finance instrument (like sustainability-linked financing instrument)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to avoid the emission of 913,600 tCO2eq, y increasing the energy efficiency and reducing Costa Rica&amp;rsquo;s HFC emissions.</narrative>
  </description>
